{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Ph6UKLJN6Fq2SPyTYhotQh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the full picture. The previous report mentions:\n1. The memory budget check may disable batching because `l_skip` is large (based on `n_logup = 24`)\n2. The temp buffer could exceed 500 MB without the budget check\n3. There was a pre-existing GPU OOM issue that prevented benchmarking\n\nSo the actual problem with the all-or-nothing approach is:\n- For the pairing benchmark, `l_skip` is large enough that the batch temp buffer exceeds the 128MB budget\n- The budget check correctly disabled batching, making the optimization a no-op\n\n\n- The optimization was never actually measured on the target benchmark\n\nThis validates the sub-batching approach—it lets us keep batching even with large `skip_domain` by constraining memory per batch. Let me dig into the full report to understand what happened before.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1973,"cache_read_input_tokens":80253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1973},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eca100d0-d51d-440d-9172-4b67f2ccfe84","uuid":"5f7eaed9-874d-471d-a4b1-8a9a9251eb37"}
