{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rz64saxm8jufSwQN7Emfa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Sub-batch Round 0 Coset-Parallel Kernel Launches\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tBatch multiple small coset-parallel AIR instances into single GPU kernel launches in Round 0,\n6\tusing sub-batching with a memory budget to avoid the all-or-nothing limitation of the previous\n7\tattempt (commit 74134b4e, reverted at 61dc6616). This directly improves SM utilization by\n8\tpacking many more thread blocks per kernel call — instead of ~1,470 serial kernel launches\n9\teach using 3-11% of 128 SMs, we get ~30-50 batched launches that saturate the GPU.\n10\t\n11\t### Critical correction to the task scope\n12\t\n13\tThe task proposes batching only `GLOBAL=false` instances (buffer_size <= 16) and leaving\n14\t`GLOBAL=true` instances (buffer_size > 16) as individual launches. However, the nsys profiling\n15\tdata shows the workload is dominated by `GLOBAL=true` coset-parallel kernels:\n16\t\n17\t| Kernel variant | Instances | GPU time | % of coset-parallel |\n18\t|---|---|---|---|\n19\t| zerocheck `<GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false>` | 539 | 221ms | 47% |\n20\t| logup `<GLOBAL=true, NEEDS_SHMEM=false>` | 396 | 196ms | 42% |\n21\t| zerocheck `<GLOBAL=false, NEEDS_SHMEM=false>` | 196 | 20ms | 4% |\n22\t| logup `<GLOBAL=false, NEEDS_SHMEM=false>` | 339 | 29ms | 6% |\n23\t| **Total** | **1,470** | **466ms** | **100%** |\n24\t\n25\tBatching only `GLOBAL=false` instances saves at most ~49ms — far short of the task's expected\n26\t270-370ms improvement. To achieve the target, `GLOBAL=true` instances (417ms) must also be\n27\tbatched. This plan includes both.\n28\t\n29\t### Why the previous all-or-nothing approach was reverted\n30\t\n31\tThe previous attempt (74134b4e) was reverted not because of a memory budget failure, but\n32\tbecause it could not be measured — a pre-existing GPU OOM bug in\n33\t`gkr_input::log_gkr_input_evals` prevented the pairing benchmark from completing. The budget\n34\tcheck (128MB) did NOT disable batching for the pairing benchmark (skip_domain=32, estimated\n35\ttemp ≈ 2.4MB). The optimization was correct (94/94 tests pass) but unmeasurable.\n36\t\n37\tSub-batching is still valuable for robustness with larger `skip_domain` values, and we extend\n38\tscope to include `GLOBAL=true` instances which the reverted commit did not handle.\n39\t\n40\t## Current Code Path\n41\t\n42\tEntry point: `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` in\n43\t`crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs:599-928`.\n44\t\n45\t```\n46\tsumcheck_uni_round0_polys()\n47\t  ├─ Lines 610-720: Setup (lambda_pows, eq_3b weights, eq_xi trees, selectors)\n48\t  ├─ Phase 1 (lines 750-841): Serial per-AIR kernel launch\n49\t  │   └─ For each of ~623 AIRs (APC 300):\n50\t  │       ├─ evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu() → zerocheck kernel\n51\t  │       │   (round0.rs:31-124 → FFI: cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:924-967)\n52\t  │       │   └─ CUDA dispatch (zerocheck_round0.cu:667-716):\n53\t  │       │       ├─ coset_parallel if (num_x * skip_domain < 32768)\n54\t  │       │       │   → grid (x_blocks, num_cosets), ~410μs avg\n55\t  │       │       └─ lockstep otherwise → grid (x_blocks, 1)\n56\t  │       │\n57\t  │       └─ evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu() → logup kernel\n58\t  │           (round0.rs:132-275 → FFI: cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs:977-1020)\n59\t  │           └─ CUDA dispatch (logup_round0.cu:658-810):\n60\t  │               ├─ coset_parallel if (num_x * skip_domain < 32768)\n61\t  │               │   → grid (x_blocks, num_cosets), ~494μs avg\n62\t  │               └─ lockstep otherwise\n63\t  │\n64\t  ├─ current_stream_sync() (line 844)\n65\t  │\n66\t  └─ Phase 2 (lines 849-924): D2H + polynomial construction\n67\t      └─ For each pending: to_host(), transpose, IDFT, build sp_0\n68\t```\n69\t\n70\tKey constants (defined in both .cu files):\n71\t- `BUFFER_THRESHOLD = 16` — GLOBAL=true above, GLOBAL=false at or below\n72\t- `COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD = 32768` — coset-parallel below, lockstep at or above\n73\t- `MAX_THREADS = 128` — block size for coset-parallel kernels\n74\t\n75\tThe `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` kernel already exists in `cuda/include/sumcheck.cuh:261`\n76\tand is used by batch_mle.cu and batch_mle_monomial.cu. We reuse it for round 0 batching.\n77\t\n78\t## Changes\n79\t\n80\t### Change 1: CUDA — Re-introduce GLOBAL=false batched kernels from 74134b4e\n81\t\n82\t**Files:**\n83\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n84\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n85\t\n86\t**What:** Cherry-pick the following from commit 74134b4e:\n87\t\n88\t1. `ZerocheckBatchMeta` struct (zerocheck_round0.cu, after line 466)\n89\t2. `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_batched_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>` kernel\n90\t3. `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched` extern \"C\" launcher\n91\t4. `LogupBatchMeta` struct (logup_round0.cu, after line 459)\n92\t5. `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_batched_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>` kernel\n93\t6. `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched` extern \"C\" launcher\n94\t\n95\tThese are exactly as in 74134b4e. They handle `GLOBAL=false` instances only (local register\n96\tbuffers, `buffer_stride=1`). The grid is `(total_x_blocks, max_num_cosets)` with per-AIR\n97\tlookup via `air_for_block[blockIdx.x]`. The reduction uses\n98\t`sumcheck::batched_final_reduce_block_sums`.\n99\t\n100\t**Why:** Proven correct (94/94 tests). Batching 535 GLOBAL=false instances eliminates ~49ms\n101\tGPU time and ~535 kernel launch calls.\n102\t\n103\t### Change 2: CUDA — Add GLOBAL=true batched kernels (new)\n104\t\n105\t**Files:**\n106\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n107\t- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n108\t\n109\t**What:** Add two new CUDA resources per file:\n110\t\n111\t1. **Extended metadata structs** (`ZerocheckBatchMetaGlobal`, `LogupBatchMetaGlobal`):\n112\t   Same as the GLOBAL=false metadata but with one additional field:\n113\t   ```cpp\n114\t   Fp *intermediates;  // pre-allocated device buffer for this AIR's intermediates\n115\t   ```\n116\t   The `buffer_stride` (= per-AIR total_threads) is computed in the kernel from\n117\t   `(segment_offsets[air_idx+1] - segment_offsets[air_idx]) * blockDim.x`, so no extra\n118\t   metadata field is needed.\n119\t\n120\t2. **Batched kernel** `zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_batched_global_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>`:\n121\t   Structurally identical to the GLOBAL=false batched kernel, with two differences:\n122\t   - Instead of `Fp local_buffer[BUFFER_THRESHOLD]`, uses:\n123\t     ```cpp\n124\t     uint32_t air_total_threads = (segment_offsets[air_idx+1] - segment_offsets[air_idx]) * blockDim.x;\n125\t     Fp *inter_buffer = meta.intermediates + (tidx * meta.buffer_size);\n126\t     uint32_t buffer_stride = air_total_threads;\n127\t     ```\n128\t   - The `NttEvalContext` uses `buffer_stride = air_total_threads` instead of `1`.\n129\t\n130\t   Same for logup: `logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_batched_global_kernel<NEEDS_SHMEM>`.\n131\t\n132\t3. **Launcher functions** `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched_global` and\n133\t   `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched_global`:\n134\t   Same signature as the GLOBAL=false launchers, plus `Fp *shared_intermediates` parameter\n135\t   (or, since intermediates pointers are in the metadata, just the same signature — the\n136\t   intermediates pointers are part of the metadata struct).\n137\t\n138\t   Actually, the intermediates are embedded in the per-AIR metadata pointer, so the launcher\n139\t   signature is identical to the GLOBAL=false version. The only difference is which kernel\n140\t   template is launched.\n141\t\n142\t**Why:** GLOBAL=true instances account for 89% (417ms) of coset-parallel GPU time. Without\n143\tbatching these, the optimization cannot achieve the target improvement. The kernel modification\n144\tis minimal — the same `acc_constraints` / `acc_interactions` functions are reused, only the\n145\tintermediates setup differs.\n146\t\n147\t### Change 3: Rust — Metadata structs and constants\n148\t\n149\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n150\t\n151\t**What:** Re-introduce from 74134b4e:\n152\t- `BUFFER_THRESHOLD`, `COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD`, `MAX_THREADS_ROUND0` constants\n153\t- `ZerocheckBatchMeta`, `LogupBatchMeta` `#[repr(C)]` structs with `unsafe impl Send`\n154\t\n155\tAdd new:\n156\t- `ZerocheckBatchMetaGlobal`, `LogupBatchMetaGlobal` `#[repr(C)]` structs — same as the\n157\t  non-global variants but with `pub intermediates: *mut F` field\n158\t\n159\t**Why:** These must match the CUDA-side struct layout exactly (`#[repr(C)]`). Separating\n160\tGLOBAL and non-GLOBAL metadata structs avoids a wasted pointer field in non-GLOBAL metadata\n161\tand keeps the CUDA kernels simple (no runtime GLOBAL check).\n162\t\n163\t### Change 4: Rust — FFI wrappers\n164\t\n165\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n166\t\n167\t**What:** Re-introduce from 74134b4e:\n168\t- `extern \"C\"` declarations for `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched` and\n169\t  `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched`\n170\t- Safe wrapper functions `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched` and\n171\t  `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched`\n172\t\n173\tAdd new:\n174\t- Same for the GLOBAL=true variants: `_zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints_batched_global`,\n175\t  `_logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0_batched_global`, and their safe wrappers\n176\t\n177\t**Why:** FFI boundary between Rust orchestration and CUDA kernels.\n178\t\n179\t### Change 5: Rust — Sub-batch orchestration in `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n180\t\n181\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, function\n182\t`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (lines 599-928)\n183\t\n184\tThis is the main logic change. Replace the per-AIR loop in Phase 1 with a three-sub-phase\n185\tstructure:\n186\t\n187\t**Sub-phase A: Classify AIRs (lines 750-841 replacement)**\n188\t\n189\tIterate over all AIRs. For each, determine:\n190\t1. `is_coset_parallel = (num_x * skip_domain) < COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD`\n191\t2. `has_constraints` / `has_interactions` (same as current)\n192\t3. `is_global_zc = zc_buffer_size > BUFFER_THRESHOLD`\n193\t4. `is_global_logup = logup_buffer_size > BUFFER_THRESHOLD`\n194\t\n195\tClassify into categories:\n196\t- **Batch-eligible GLOBAL=false zerocheck**: `is_coset_parallel && has_constraints && !is_global_zc`\n197\t- **Batch-eligible GLOBAL=true zerocheck**: `is_coset_parallel && has_constraints && is_global_zc`\n198\t- **Batch-eligible GLOBAL=false logup**: `is_coset_parallel && has_interactions && !is_global_logup`\n199\t- **Batch-eligible GLOBAL=true logup**: `is_coset_parallel && has_interactions && is_global_logup`\n200\t- **Individual**: `!is_coset_parallel` (lockstep) — launch immediately as today\n201\t\n202\tFor batch-eligible AIRs, collect metadata into vectors (same structure as 74134b4e Sub-phase A,\n203\textended with GLOBAL=true metadata). For logup, compute per-AIR DAG, weights, and d_rules\n204\tinline (same as 74134b4e).\n205\t\n206\tStore per-AIR x_blocks for grouping: `x_blocks = (num_x * skip_domain).div_ceil(block_x)`.\n207\t\n208\tFor GLOBAL=true AIRs, also compute and pre-allocate the intermediates buffer:\n209\t- `intermed_size = buffer_size * air_total_threads` where `air_total_threads = x_blocks * block_x`\n210\t- Allocate from a shared intermediates buffer (one DeviceBuffer per GLOBAL=true sub-batch)\n211\t\n212\t**Sub-phase B: Form sub-batches**\n213\t\n214\tFor each of the 4 batch categories (zerocheck/logup x GLOBAL/non-GLOBAL):\n215\t\n216\t```rust\n217\tconst PER_BATCH_TMP_BUDGET: usize = 32 * 1024 * 1024; // 32 MB\n218\t\n219\tlet d = max_num_cosets * skip_domain;\n220\tlet elem_size = size_of::<EF>(); // or size_of::<Frac<EF>>() for logup\n221\t\n222\tlet mut sub_batches = vec![];\n223\tlet mut current_batch = vec![];\n224\tlet mut current_total_x_blocks: u32 = 0;\n225\t\n226\tfor (idx, meta, x_blocks) in eligible_airs {\n227\t    let projected_tmp = (current_total_x_blocks + x_blocks) as usize * d * elem_size;\n228\t    if projected_tmp > PER_BATCH_TMP_BUDGET && !current_batch.is_empty() {\n229\t        sub_batches.push(current_batch);\n230\t        current_batch = vec![];\n231\t        current_total_x_blocks = 0;\n232\t    }\n233\t    current_batch.push((idx, meta, x_blocks));\n234\t    current_total_x_blocks += x_blocks;\n235\t}\n236\tif !current_batch.is_empty() {\n237\t    sub_batches.push(current_batch);\n238\t}\n239\t```\n240\t\n241\tFor the pairing benchmark at APC 300 (skip_domain=32, d≈128):\n242\t- GLOBAL=true zerocheck (539 AIRs): total_x_blocks ≈ 539 (most have 1 block)\n243\t  - tmp per batch = 539 * 128 * 16 = 1.1 MB → 1 sub-batch\n244\t- GLOBAL=true logup (396 AIRs): tmp ≈ 0.8 MB → 1 sub-batch\n245\t- GLOBAL=false zerocheck (196 AIRs): tmp ≈ 0.4 MB → 1 sub-batch\n246\t- GLOBAL=false logup (339 AIRs): tmp ≈ 0.7 MB → 1 sub-batch\n247\t- **Total: ~4 batched launches** (plus ~30-40 lockstep individual launches)\n248\t\n249\tFor large skip_domain (e.g., skip_domain=2048, d=8192):\n250\t- tmp per 32 AIRs = 32 * 8192 * 16 = 4.2 MB → many more sub-batches\n251\t- Sub-batching ensures memory stays bounded\n252\t\n253\t**Sub-phase C: Launch sub-batches**\n254\t\n255\tFor each sub-batch, reusing the pattern from 74134b4e:\n256\t\n257\t1. Build `air_for_block` and `segment_offsets` arrays (same `build_batch_arrays` helper)\n258\t2. H2D transfer metadata, air_for_block, segment_offsets (small, <10μs each)\n259\t3. Allocate or reuse temp buffer (`fill_zero()` required)\n260\t4. Launch batched evaluation kernel (GLOBAL=false or GLOBAL=true variant)\n261\t5. Launch `batched_final_reduce_block_sums` reduction kernel\n262\t   - Output into global output buffer at `batch_air_offset * d`\n263\t6. Drop temp buffer (freed for next sub-batch)\n264\t\n265\tFor GLOBAL=true sub-batches, additionally:\n266\t7. Allocate shared intermediates buffer: `sum(buffer_size_i * air_total_threads_i) * sizeof(Fp)`\n267\t8. Set `meta.intermediates` for each AIR to its offset in the shared buffer\n268\t9. Drop intermediates buffer after kernel launch (not needed after sync)\n269\t\n270\tThe output buffer is pre-allocated for all batched AIRs in each category:\n271\t- `d_zc_global_output: DeviceBuffer<EF>` of size `num_zc_global_batched * d`\n272\t- `d_zc_local_output: DeviceBuffer<EF>` of size `num_zc_local_batched * d`\n273\t- Same for logup with `Frac<EF>`\n274\t\n275\t**Temp buffer reuse optimization:** Pre-allocate one temp buffer sized for the largest\n276\tsub-batch. Reuse across sub-batches with `fill_zero()` between launches. This avoids\n277\trepeated `DeviceBuffer::with_capacity` calls. Cost: one `fill_zero()` per sub-batch (~0.1ms).\n278\t\n279\t**Phase 2 modification:** Extend the `Round0Pending` struct with batch category info:\n280\t\n281\t```rust\n282\tstruct Round0Pending<F, EF> {\n283\t    // ... existing fields ...\n284\t    zc_batch_info: Option<(BatchCategory, usize)>,  // (category, index_in_category)\n285\t    logup_batch_info: Option<(BatchCategory, usize)>,\n286\t}\n287\t\n288\tenum BatchCategory { GlobalTrue, GlobalFalse }\n289\t```\n290\t\n291\tIn Phase 2, after `current_stream_sync()`:\n292\t1. D2H all 4 output buffers (zc_global, zc_local, logup_global, logup_local)\n293\t2. For each pending AIR, extract the correct slice based on batch_info\n294\t3. Feed into existing polynomial construction (unchanged)\n295\t\n296\t### Change 6: Keep-alive buffers\n297\t\n298\t**File:** `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n299\t\n300\tFor all batch-eligible AIRs, device buffers containing per-AIR data must remain alive until\n301\t`current_stream_sync()`:\n302\t- `d_main_parts_vec` — already handled in current code\n303\t- Logup per-AIR `d_rules`, `d_numer_weights`, `d_denom_weights` — keep-alive vectors as in\n304\t  74134b4e\n305\t- GLOBAL=true shared `intermediates` buffers — one per sub-batch, held in a Vec until sync\n306\t\n307\tDrop all keep-alive buffers after `current_stream_sync()` and before Phase 2 D2H transfers.\n308\t\n309\t## Invariants\n310\t\n311\t1. **Correctness**: For every AIR, the batched kernel must produce the same output as the\n312\t   individual kernel for the same inputs. This follows from the batched kernel being\n313\t   structurally identical to the single-AIR kernel — same `acc_constraints`/`acc_interactions`\n314\t   logic, same NTT evaluation, same reduction. The only difference is thread block assignment.\n315\t\n316\t2. **Output layout**: Batched output is `[num_airs_in_batch][d]` where\n317\t   `d = max_num_cosets * skip_domain`. For AIRs with `num_cosets < max_num_cosets`, the extra\n318\t   coset entries are zero (early-return blocks write nothing, temp buffer is zero-filled).\n319\t   Phase 2 reads only `num_cosets * skip_domain` elements per AIR, so padding is harmless.\n320\t\n321\t3. **Memory safety**: All device pointers in metadata structs (selectors_cube, preprocessed,\n322\t   main_parts, eq_cube, d_rules, etc.) must remain valid until `current_stream_sync()`.\n323\t   This is guaranteed by the keep-alive vectors.\n324\t\n325\t4. **GLOBAL=true intermediates**: Each thread in the batched kernel must access its own\n326\t   `buffer_size` slots at stride `air_total_threads`, matching the non-batched kernel's\n327\t   layout. The pre-allocated intermediates buffer must be large enough for\n328\t   `sum(buffer_size_i * air_total_threads_i)` across all AIRs in the sub-batch.\n329\t\n330\t5. **Lockstep fallback**: AIRs with `num_x * skip_domain >= COSET_PARALLEL_THRESHOLD` are\n331\t   NOT batched and continue to use individual lockstep kernel launches. This preserves\n332\t   correctness for large AIRs.\n333\t\n334\t6. **Verifier unchanged**: No protocol changes. The polynomial values produced in Phase 2 are\n335\t   identical; only the GPU computation path differs.\n336\t\n337\t## Measurement Plan\n338\t\n339\tIn the powdr repo:\n340\t\n341\t```bash\n342\t# Before changes: capture baseline for this task\n343\tfor apc in 0 100 300; do\n344\t  openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # with APC=$apc\n345\t  cp results/pairing/apc${apc}/metrics.json \\\n346\t     ../stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-11-1145-subbatch-round0-coset-parallel/results/before_apc${apc}.json\n347\tdone\n348\t\n349\t# After changes: capture results\n350\tfor apc in 0 100 300; do\n351\t  openvm-riscv/scripts/run_pairing.sh  # with APC=$apc\n352\t  cp results/pairing/apc${apc}/metrics.json \\\n353\t     ../stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-11-1145-subbatch-round0-coset-parallel/results/after_apc${apc}.json\n354\tdone\n355\t\n356\t# Combined metrics\n357\tpython basic_metrics.py \\\n358\t  autoopt-results/2026-04-11-1145-subbatch-round0-coset-parallel/results/after_apc*.json \\\n359\t  > autoopt-results/2026-04-11-1145-subbatch-round0-coset-parallel/results/metrics_combined.json\n360\t\n361\t# Analysis\n362\tpython spec.py <combined_json> <experiment_name>\n363\t```\n364\t\n365\tRun all tests:\n366\t```bash\n367\tcargo nextest run -p openvm-cuda-backend --test-threads=4\n368\t```\n369\t\n370\tNsight profiling (if needed for detailed kernel analysis):\n371\t```bash\n372\tnsys profile --trace=cuda --output=nsys_after \\\n373\t  <pairing_benchmark_command>\n374\tnsys stats nsys_after.nsys-rep --report cuda_gpu_kern_sum\n375\t```\n376\t\n377\tKey metrics to compare:\n378\t- Round 0 wall time (from metrics.json)\n379\t- STARK excl trace (from metrics.json)\n380\t- Number of kernel launches (from nsight)\n381\t- SM occupancy (from nsight)\n382\t\n383\t## Rollback Criteria\n384\t\n385\tRevert if any of these conditions hold after full implementation:\n386\t\n387\t1. **No improvement**: Round 0 APC 300 >= 540ms (within 5% of current 569ms)\n388\t2. **Regression at APC 0**: STARK excl trace APC 0 increases by > 20ms\n389\t3. **Test failures**: Any of the 94 `openvm-cuda-backend` tests fail\n390\t4. **GPU OOM**: Batched temp/intermediates buffers cause out-of-memory on RTX 4090 (24GB)\n391\t5. **Proof verification failure**: Generated proofs fail verification for any APC config\n392\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qv3gTc3kgiTnVk6vFjTDsC","session_id":"eca100d0-d51d-440d-9172-4b67f2ccfe84","uuid":"16720c3f-73d4-4ac2-ba8b-84783cf0980a","timestamp":"2026-04-11T08:44:24.184Z"}
