ince threads with `coset_idx >= meta.num_cosets` return early and never touch the intermediates buffer anyway.\n\nCalculating the stride... I'm checking whether using `max_num_cosets` versus `meta.num_cosets` for the stride actually matters — threads with `coset_idx >= meta.num_cosets` early-return anyway, so the stride choice only affects memory usage, not correctness. Using `meta.num_cosets` saves memory but requires reading metadata, while `max_num_cosets` wastes some space but keeps the kernel simpler.\n\nNow I'm laying out the specific fixes needed: correcting the GLOBAL intermediates layout with proper coset-dimension striding, removing the contradictory \"drop intermediates\" note, including intermediates in the memory budget, spelling out the per-AIR offset calculation explicitly, and making sure the logup DAG and weight hoisting strategy is clearly specified.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4536,"cache_read_input_tokens":114125,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4536},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eca100d0-d51d-440d-9172-4b67f2ccfe84","uuid":"caaa09ad-0ed8-4e68-9326-c02ebd5c7b12"}
